{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Tithe you shall tithe.</b> This section is juxtaposed here because above he prohibited eating unclean species; afterward he comes to prohibit eating meat, grain, new wine, and oil of the holy — except in the chosen place." "<b>Tithe you shall tithe.</b> To include merchandise. Another interpretation: <b>tithe you shall tithe</b> — one might say that anything that grows from the earth, such as flax-stalks and patches of thorns, should be liable to tithe; Scripture says, ״עשר תעשר ואכלת״ — one might say even honey and milk should be liable to tithe; Scripture says, ״היצא השדה שנה שנה״. <b>The produce of the field</b> — to exclude an unperforated planter-box, which does not draw sustenance from the field. This section has already been stated three times, and each time it is repeated it is for a matter newly introduced in it, as Rashi explained; and now it is repeated for the matter of the redemption of second tithe, as it is written, ״ונתת בכסף״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:49.256236837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}